/// Object Identity Link (OIL)
/// Description
/// Candidate links between the identifiers two catalogs give the same space
/// object: a provider's own number and a NORAD catalog number, an
/// international designator, or another provider's number (for example a JSC
/// Vimpel number and a NORAD number). A link is a declaration with its
/// evidence, never an assertion: it says which source declared the pairing,
/// in which edition and on which line, how often, with what first-detection
/// dates, and whether the pairing is one-to-one or part of a group where one
/// identifier is declared against several on the other side (an alias or a
/// conflict). A consumer binds identities only after testing the link, for
/// example by comparing trajectories ($XMT), and records the outcome in the
/// link's STATUS.
///
